1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,560
<i>Now that's scary.</i>

4
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,550
<i>She's probably using magic
that cuts through physical objects.</i>

5
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:28,500
<i>It's a simple type of magic,
but I can't see its trajectory.</i>

6
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:35,730
It's impossible to block all of them, but...

7
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,270
What's the matter? You're not
going to follow up on that?

8
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:42,150
I might've gone a bit too hard.

9
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,000
Maybe.

10
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:48,120
The range of your magic is
about five meters, isn't it?

11
00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:51,700
Correct. So, what do we do now?

12
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:54,430
Are we going to whale on each
other with basic spells again?

13
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:58,080
No, that won't be necessary.

14
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:01,510
<i>His magic is devoid of character.</i>

15
00:01:01,510 --> 00:01:03,730
<i>It's underhanded,
for the sole purpose of winning.</i>

16
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:08,030
<i>The girl fighting Wirbel now
will probably be killed.</i>

17
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:11,150
Now, then.

18
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:18,120
<i>A saturation attack?</i>

19
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:24,970
<i>How can she control so many
attack spells at once?</i>

20
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:30,390
This is an absurd feat of strength.

21
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:32,210
It doesn't have a shred of character.

22
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:37,700
I can't... handle them all.

23
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:20,000
Sorganeil.

24
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,820
I can't move.

25
00:03:32,370 --> 00:03:34,740
<i>I can't control my mana, either.</i>

26
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:38,040
<i>It's a powerful binding spell.</i>

27
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:42,060
<i>If he has this, why didn't
he catch a Stille himself?</i>

28
00:03:42,990 --> 00:03:47,340
<i>Though I suppose it's useless
if he can't find one.</i>

29
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:52,270
My spell binds those I can see.

30
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:56,980
As long as I keep looking at you,
you won't be able to move.

31
00:03:57,250 --> 00:04:01,580
I could easily kill you in your current state.

32
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:04,980
<i>Not only that, but he was holding back.</i>

33
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:07,620
<i>If he'd truly intended to kill me,</i>

34
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:10,850
<i>he would've bound me during his initial ambush.</i>

35
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:13,490
This is your last chance.

36
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:18,210
Leave the Stille and walk away.

37
00:04:19,510 --> 00:04:21,840
<i>Aw, he's no fun.</i>

38
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:24,540
<i>And I thought I'd finally
found a fight to the death.</i>

39
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:28,040
<i>So threatening me into handing over
our Stille was his goal after all.</i>

40
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,700
Wait a minute.

41
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:34,760
Why do you need to order me to do that?

42
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:38,520
You could just take the Stille
from me while I couldn't move.

43
00:04:58,750 --> 00:05:02,570
So you need to keep my entire body in view.

44
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:05,460
No wonder you don't use it
against multiple targets.

45
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,550
You were aiming for my eyes.

46
00:05:07,550 --> 00:05:09,750
That's the logical choice, isn't it?

47
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:15,130
No. If I were you, I'd go for
the kill and attack the neck.

48
00:05:15,130 --> 00:05:17,430
That would end the fight.

49
00:05:17,990 --> 00:05:20,280
You should've been able to do that.

50
00:05:21,230 --> 00:05:24,510
There were people on the battlefield
who did similar things.

51
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:29,780
They were all perverts who enjoyed killing.

52
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:35,280
I guess I should kill you now.

53
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:40,720
Have you ever killed women
and children before?

54
00:05:41,350 --> 00:05:43,110
You think I haven't?

55
00:05:43,790 --> 00:05:48,040
Huh. What hells have you seen?

56
00:05:48,470 --> 00:05:50,230
Trying to buy time?

57
00:05:52,230 --> 00:05:54,770
Fine. I'll play along.

58
00:05:57,320 --> 00:06:02,020
The Northern Magic Corps are mercenaries
who specialize in fighting demons,

59
00:06:02,690 --> 00:06:05,910
but in times of need, we're mobilized
to fight in wars between nations.

60
00:06:09,610 --> 00:06:13,550
People know exactly what makes
other people weak.

61
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:20,960
The fiendish act of sending women
and children to war wasn't uncommon.

62
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:23,220
It wasn't hell.

63
00:06:25,050 --> 00:06:27,120
It's commonplace in the far north.

64
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:31,600
I see. I've heard enough.

65
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,910
You're not going to kill me?

66
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:56,500
I think the magic a person specializes in
is strongly related to their life and nature.

67
00:06:57,040 --> 00:07:03,370
A spell that binds your opponent feels like
a way to delay killing them.

68
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:09,350
I see. That's why you let me buy time, too.

69
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:11,530
I'm surprised.

70
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:17,020
Your hands are already drenched in blood,
and yet you still want to remain human.

71
00:07:20,150 --> 00:07:24,480
That's right. I use this time
to prepare myself to kill.

72
00:07:25,290 --> 00:07:26,750
But you know, miss...

73
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:34,880
Though I may hesitate,
I've always killed everyone I had to.

74
00:07:38,150 --> 00:07:40,080
Later, miss.

75
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,740
Don't move.

76
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:53,260
You're kidding, right?

77
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:55,310
You beat Ehre?

78
00:07:55,310 --> 00:07:57,590
<i>I didn't sense her at all.</i>

79
00:07:58,270 --> 00:08:01,890
I'm surprised. You can
completely conceal your mana?

80
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,560
You must be the one who captured the Stille.

81
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:07,660
We just got lucky.

82
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:10,450
We happened upon a Stille's roost,

83
00:08:10,450 --> 00:08:14,430
and her master had taught her
a spell that captures a bird.

84
00:08:14,430 --> 00:08:19,580
And you've got a spell that binds anything,
so I guess you just got really unlucky.

85
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:22,310
Seriously. I've got no luck.

86
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,080
You were fighting Ehre.

87
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,330
What happened to her?

88
00:08:26,610 --> 00:08:27,820
I killed her.

89
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:35,490
The conditions for passing the first test

90
00:08:35,490 --> 00:08:42,010
are possessing a Stille by sunset tonight
and having all your party members present.

91
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:47,820
We lost. I'm getting out of here.

92
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:51,140
I thought you were going to kill me.

93
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:53,740
I've already failed the test.

94
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:55,900
Killing you would be unnecessary.

95
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:56,870
Later.

96
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:01,720
You can attack me from behind if you want.

97
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:06,490
You'll just be turning an unnecessary kill
back into a necessary one.

98
00:09:06,510 --> 00:09:07,690
Ms. Übel.

99
00:09:08,230 --> 00:09:09,620
I know.

100
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:17,000
You're a good liar.

101
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,890
We should go to assist
Mr. Land while we can.

102
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:25,440
That four-eyes will be fine.
He's quite the pretender.

103
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,280
It's over.

104
00:09:42,730 --> 00:09:44,560
This is impressive.

105
00:09:47,070 --> 00:09:51,040
You turned countless petals into metal
and controlled them precisely

106
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,670
to slip them through my defenses.

107
00:09:54,460 --> 00:09:56,580
But this is your own invention, isn't it?

108
00:09:56,580 --> 00:10:01,300
Spells like that often
neglect the fundamentals.

109
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:08,190
I always watch and wait when
fighting an opponent I don't know.

110
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:11,410
I know exactly what your weaknesses are.

111
00:10:11,410 --> 00:10:13,570
I'll probably win.

112
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:15,340
Talkative, aren't you?

113
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:18,560
How do you intend to win when
I've ruined your dominant arm?

114
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:25,040
If you won't surrender,
then I'll take your head off.

115
00:10:25,310 --> 00:10:29,300
I told you, I'm still observing you
before the battle begins.

116
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:32,660
You're not very good at
detecting mana, are you?

117
00:10:41,850 --> 00:10:43,430
Illusion magic.

118
00:10:43,430 --> 00:10:46,920
It has substance, so strictly speaking,
it's more like a clone.

119
00:10:48,890 --> 00:10:50,040
How long—

120
00:10:53,370 --> 00:10:57,790
Since the beginning,
when the first test started.

121
00:10:58,650 --> 00:11:00,950
I don't trust other people.

122
00:11:04,410 --> 00:11:06,410
Killed her, my ass.

123
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:10,250
That bitch lied like it was nothing.

124
00:11:11,150 --> 00:11:12,970
Wake up, Ehre.

125
00:11:15,530 --> 00:11:18,390
Out of mana? Pathetic.

126
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:20,420
Didn't you graduate at the top of your class?

127
00:11:21,850 --> 00:11:25,630
She overwhelmed me with
ordinary offensive magic.

128
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:28,300
I couldn't block them all.

129
00:11:30,230 --> 00:11:32,310
You don't believe me, do you?

130
00:11:33,310 --> 00:11:34,680
No, I do.

131
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:43,310
Why'd you attack her head-on like an idiot?

132
00:11:43,310 --> 00:11:46,450
It's not like you couldn't have won.

133
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:53,380
<i>But if she could pull off this stunt
with ordinary offensive magic alone,</i>

134
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:56,940
<i>she must be one nasty monster.</i>

135
00:11:58,040 --> 00:12:01,130
Let's go. We'll meet up with Scharf.

136
00:12:01,130 --> 00:12:03,940
Wait. I can't walk.

137
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:06,660
Oh, fine.

138
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:14,690
Are you really going to float me
there like an object?

139
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:15,890
Carry me on your back!

140
00:12:20,630 --> 00:12:23,020
Why am I doing this?

141
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:25,300
Do you sense Scharf nearby?

142
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:27,580
He's on the other side of those bushes.

143
00:12:28,270 --> 00:12:31,710
Hey, Scharf. Help me carry...

144
00:12:35,610 --> 00:12:38,610
Wirbel, carry me on your back.

145
00:12:38,610 --> 00:12:40,670
I feel numb and can't move.

146
00:12:45,110 --> 00:12:46,340
Damn it.

147
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:48,420
Seriously, what the hell is going on?

148
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:53,930
What's this sound?

149
00:12:53,930 --> 00:12:55,760
Probably the rain.

150
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:58,230
It's started raining outside the barrier.

151
00:12:58,990 --> 00:13:01,650
It's like my current mental state.

152
00:13:01,650 --> 00:13:04,480
The sun will set in two or three more hours.

153
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,630
The first test will end.

154
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:09,500
Two of us are out of the fight.

155
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:12,600
We can't steal anyone's Stille like this.

156
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:15,160
We're going to fail.

157
00:13:15,790 --> 00:13:20,010
But you're helping us anyway.
You're a nice guy.

158
00:13:20,010 --> 00:13:23,110
I don't mind ditching you
two here, you know.

159
00:13:23,110 --> 00:13:24,470
Please don't abandon us.

160
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:26,690
Don't cry. You're a man, aren't you?

161
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:33,100
Is that kindness the reason
you fight demons?

162
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:41,160
You saved my village, too.

163
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:42,180
Are you stupid?

164
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:45,700
I couldn't risk my life for kindness.

165
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:48,620
People fight for their own desires.

166
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:51,830
In my case, I had ulterior motives.

167
00:13:52,310 --> 00:13:54,750
I was in love with a girl from my hometown.

168
00:13:56,250 --> 00:14:02,820
Exactly 29 years ago, the demon activity
in the northern lands increased.

169
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:06,010
She and her entire family
fled to the central lands.

170
00:14:06,590 --> 00:14:08,630
I was a dumb kid.

171
00:14:08,630 --> 00:14:10,590
I decided to show off for her.

172
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:15,070
I'll kill all those shitty demons.

173
00:14:15,070 --> 00:14:17,930
When I do, come back to this village.

174
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:26,690
I was only four or five years old.

175
00:14:27,220 --> 00:14:29,600
I don't even remember
her face or name anymore.

176
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:35,860
What an idiot.

177
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:37,810
Yeah. I'm an idiot.

178
00:14:44,690 --> 00:14:49,180
Are we sailing back home again?
I get seasick easily.

179
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:52,410
Want me to introduce you to my grandpa?

180
00:14:52,410 --> 00:14:54,900
Since he's a first-class mage,
we can travel by land to...

181
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,540
Hey, Wirbel.

182
00:14:58,030 --> 00:14:58,990
What is it?

183
00:14:58,990 --> 00:15:00,060
Look.

184
00:15:11,790 --> 00:15:15,570
You can't be serious.
What was all that effort for?

185
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:19,760
Took long enough for luck to go my way.

186
00:15:25,970 --> 00:15:29,660
Frieren, she's not doing anything.

187
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,130
<i>An elf, huh?</i>

188
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:37,130
<i>She's a skilled mage.</i>

189
00:15:37,430 --> 00:15:42,580
<i>I doubt Laufen's magic would work a
second time now that she's seen it.</i>

190
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:45,580
<i>But just once was enough.</i>

191
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:48,140
<i>We're not trying to kill each other here.</i>

192
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:51,910
She vanished?

193
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:54,110
Frieren, the Stille...

194
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:57,160
She took it, huh?

195
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:04,980
That's an interesting spell.

196
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:20,380
It's comfortable inside the barrier
even when it's raining.

197
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:25,110
Come to think of it, aren't you the proctor
for the second test, Sense?

198
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:31,220
Looks like you killed a few promising
test-takers again, Genau.

199
00:16:32,510 --> 00:16:33,980
Don't make me laugh.

200
00:16:35,790 --> 00:16:38,970
No promising test-taker would die from this.

201
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:43,570
Besides, first-class mages
simply have that much worth.

202
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:46,360
You should know that.

203
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:55,170
Either way, choosing a target immune to
mana detection for a mage test wasn't nice.

204
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:58,390
Whether or not they'll catch one
comes down to luck.

205
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:02,630
This is a battle masquerading
as a competition.

206
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,940
Luck is a skill.

207
00:17:05,310 --> 00:17:10,200
And some test-takers seem to have captured
a Stille without relying on luck.

208
00:17:11,490 --> 00:17:14,320
The sun will set in three hours.

209
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:17,580
The battle will grow more intense.

210
00:17:20,670 --> 00:17:22,930
Who do you think will survive?

211
00:17:22,930 --> 00:17:25,160
A third will remain.

212
00:17:25,430 --> 00:17:28,590
Denken will be among them.

213
00:17:28,590 --> 00:17:32,800
His skill is comparable
to a first-class mage's.

214
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:36,550
What's an old man only interested
in wealth and political power

215
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:38,890
doing getting certified now?

216
00:17:38,890 --> 00:17:41,200
Is he doing it for the privilege after all?

217
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,560
Who knows?

218
00:17:42,890 --> 00:17:45,370
He's getting up there in years.

219
00:17:45,370 --> 00:17:47,720
I'm sure he's got something on his mind.

220
00:17:48,550 --> 00:17:53,310
The spell that girl used
was Jilwer, wasn't it?

221
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:57,700
That's a folk spell used by a mountain tribe
in the southern lands.

222
00:17:58,060 --> 00:17:59,960
That's right.

223
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:01,720
What's a Jilwer?

224
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,590
A spell that allows you to move at high speed.

225
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:08,070
Then the two of you
should've remained hidden.

226
00:18:08,650 --> 00:18:11,580
She could've simply taken
the Stille on her own.

227
00:18:11,810 --> 00:18:17,360
Laufen is still inexperienced.
She left too many traces of mana behind.

228
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:21,710
You could have easily followed her, Frieren.

229
00:18:23,050 --> 00:18:26,640
You must really find
our presence troublesome.

230
00:18:26,890 --> 00:18:30,390
Well, yes. You know who I am?

231
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:35,040
There isn't a mage of our generation
who doesn't know that name.

232
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:38,020
It's my first time seeing
you with my own eyes,

233
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:40,270
but I knew who you were
as soon as I saw you.

234
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:45,280
You are Frieren, the mage
from the party of heroes.

235
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:46,960
Is she famous?

236
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:51,700
She's a legendary mage.
I knew it might be possible, but...

237
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:54,300
I guess elves really don't age.

238
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:57,460
You're challenging me rather openly.

239
00:18:57,460 --> 00:19:00,420
You've been sniffing around us
this whole time, haven't you?

240
00:19:00,810 --> 00:19:03,680
I was expecting something underhanded.

241
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:06,170
This is plenty underhanded.

242
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:13,050
While Denken keeps you busy,
I'll kill one of those two kids.

243
00:19:13,350 --> 00:19:14,810
I see.

244
00:19:14,810 --> 00:19:21,320
If we can't pass because we're lacking a
party member, we'll be forced to back off.

245
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:23,910
Interesting. Try me.

246
00:19:23,910 --> 00:19:26,100
Lawine, he's strong.

247
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:27,450
I know.

248
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:35,050
Don't, Richter. All we need
to do is keep them busy.

249
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:36,200
We can win this fight.

250
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:43,220
Denken, I thought you were a
more merciless and cold man.

251
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:45,720
You're an imperial mage, aren't you?

252
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:49,290
I'm sure you've killed political enemies
more than a couple of times.

253
00:19:57,580 --> 00:20:02,480
I simply don't believe being a first-class mage
is worth killing someone.

254
00:20:02,790 --> 00:20:05,110
I can agree with that.

255
00:20:05,110 --> 00:20:08,130
"First-class mage" is just a title.

256
00:20:08,130 --> 00:20:10,370
It's not that valuable.

257
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:14,170
You can't be serious.

258
00:20:14,170 --> 00:20:17,470
You mean you took this test without
knowing the privilege that title grants?

259
00:20:17,470 --> 00:20:18,370
Privilege?

260
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:25,360
More than fifty years ago,
the great mage and founder

261
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:31,040
of the Continental Magic Association,
Serie, suddenly appeared

262
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:33,440
to reign over humanity's magic.

263
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:41,190
She's still searching for mages refined
during the long war against the Demon King.

264
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:46,490
So she promised to grant a special
privilege to anyone who achieved

265
00:20:46,490 --> 00:20:49,080
the rank of first-class mage.

266
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:53,820
She will grant them any
one spell they desire.

267
00:20:54,870 --> 00:21:00,780
Serie is a living grimoire who knows nearly
every spell in humanity's history.

268
00:21:00,780 --> 00:21:05,470
She's the closest mage in our world to the
all-knowing and all-powerful Goddess.

269
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,340
You could acquire massive wealth,

270
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:13,400
cure the gravest of diseases,
or gain overwhelming power.

271
00:21:14,660 --> 00:21:20,880
For mages, to gain whatever spell they want
is equivalent to having a wish granted.

272
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:23,410
People are simple.

273
00:21:23,410 --> 00:21:28,420
So modern first-class mages are all
monsters who barely seem human.

274
00:21:29,190 --> 00:21:31,270
It's that valuable a privilege.

275
00:21:31,830 --> 00:21:32,720
I see.

276
00:21:33,410 --> 00:21:34,800
This is nonsense.

277
00:21:38,910 --> 00:21:44,040
Denken, people like you who don't care
about the privilege are the minority.

278
00:21:45,550 --> 00:21:47,060
Let's begin.

279
00:21:47,060 --> 00:21:49,920
Denken, keep her busy for one minute.

280
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:52,390
That's enough time for me
to kill the two of them.

281
00:21:52,390 --> 00:21:54,820
Don't make me say it again, Richter.

282
00:21:55,120 --> 00:21:57,200
They're just kids.

283
00:21:57,200 --> 00:22:00,050
We're simply going to put them
to sleep for three hours.

284
00:22:00,050 --> 00:22:02,360
You can handle looking after
some children, can't you?

285
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,320
Denken.

286
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:10,170
I'll crush her.

287
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:12,270
That should be enough.

288
00:22:12,650 --> 00:22:14,280
You old fart.

289
00:22:15,430 --> 00:22:16,780
Bargland.

290
00:22:35,380 --> 00:22:38,970
The young are too hot-blooded.

291
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:22,120
You inexperienced fool.

292
00:24:20,610 --> 00:24:22,120
What spell do I desire?

293
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:23,280
The difference between our mana is too great.

294
00:24:21,370 --> 00:24:23,290
But she underestimates us.

295
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:23,640
Give me a break.

296
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:26,000
That old man fights rather spectacularly.

297
00:24:23,840 --> 00:24:24,600
I know!

298
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:25,690
This is Frieren.

299
00:24:25,690 --> 00:24:29,920
In the world of magic, sometimes
the world is turned upside down.
